gartner-hypecycle-graph: 1
# A hand-authored hype cycle of how warfare is changing, centred on the war in Ukraine, with ideas
# that have not started yet. Dates after 2026 are projections, and dates and influences are
# illustrative, not a claim: see readme.md.
trends:
  - id: precision-guided-munitions
    name: Precision-guided munitions
    start: 1972-05
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 0
    phases: 4
    tags: [strike]
    description: Laser-guided bombs from 1972, satellite-guided ones from the late 1990s.
  - id: gps
    name: GPS
    start: 1978-02
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 2
    phases: 4
    tags: [navigation, space]
  - id: network-centric-warfare
    name: Network-centric warfare
    start: 1998-01
    stop: 2020-01
    row: 4
    phases: 3
    tags: [command]
    description: The doctrine that linking sensors and shooters beats massing forces.
  - id: armed-drones
    name: Armed military drones
    start: 2001-10
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 6
    phases: 4
    tags: [drones]
    description: From the armed Predator of 2001 on.
  - id: cyber-warfare
    name: Cyber warfare
    start: 2007-04
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 8
    phases: 3
    tags: [cyber]
    description: From the attacks on Estonia in 2007 on.
  - id: hybrid-warfare
    name: Hybrid warfare
    start: 2014-02
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 12
    phases: 3
    tags: [doctrine]
    description: Unmarked troops, disinformation and proxies in Crimea and the Donbas.
  - id: commercial-satellite-imagery
    name: Commercial satellite imagery
    start: 2014-01
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 10
    phases: 3
    tags: [space, intelligence]
  - id: open-source-intelligence
    name: Open-source intelligence
    start: 2014-07
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 16
    phases: 3
    tags: [intelligence]
    description: Public photos and videos turned into evidence, from the MH17 investigation on.
  - id: electronic-warfare
    name: Electronic warfare
    start: 2014-04
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 14
    phases: 2
    tags: [ew]
    description: Jamming and spoofing of radios, drones and satellite navigation.
  - id: strike-drones
    name: Medium-altitude strike drones
    start: 2020-09
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 18
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2022-06
    tags: [drones]
    description: Drones like the Bayraktar TB2, celebrated in 2020 and early 2022, then vulnerable to air defence.
  - id: loitering-munitions
    name: Loitering munitions
    start: 2020-09
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 20
    phases: 2
    tags: [drones, strike]
  - id: anti-tank-missiles
    name: Man-portable anti-tank missiles
    start: 2022-02
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 22
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2022-09
    tags: [infantry]
    description: Javelin and NLAW in the first weeks of the invasion.
  - id: satellite-communications
    name: Satellite communications at the front
    start: 2022-02
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 24
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2022-10
    tags: [space, command]
    description: Starlink terminals kept units connected after the KA-SAT network was hacked on the first day.
  - id: battlefield-management-software
    name: Battlefield management software
    start: 2022-03
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 26
    phases: 1
    tags: [command, software]
    description: Systems such as Delta that fuse drone video, reports and maps into one picture.
  - id: rocket-artillery
    name: Long-range precision rocket artillery
    start: 2022-06
    stop: 2032-01
    row: 28
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2023-03
    tags: [strike]
    description: HIMARS, decisive in 2022 until jamming blunted its guided rockets.
  - id: fpv-drones
    name: FPV strike drones
    start: 2022-09
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 30
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2024-06
    tags: [drones]
    description: Cheap racing drones carrying a charge, flown by goggle-wearing pilots.
  - id: long-range-attack-drones
    name: Long-range one-way attack drones
    start: 2022-09
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 32
    phases: 1
    tags: [drones, strike]
    description: Shahed-type drones fired in waves against cities and power plants.
  - id: sea-drones
    name: Uncrewed surface vessels
    start: 2022-10
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 34
    phases: 1
    tags: [drones, naval]
    description: Ukraine's sea drones pushed the Black Sea Fleet away from western Crimea.
  - id: layered-air-defence
    name: Layered air defence
    start: 2022-10
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 36
    phases: 1
    tags: [air-defence]
    description: Patriot and IRIS-T high up, mobile gun teams against drones low down.
  - id: transparent-battlefield
    name: The transparent battlefield
    start: 2023-06
    stop: 2032-01
    row: 38
    phases: 1
    tags: [doctrine]
    description: Constant surveillance made massed manoeuvre costly, and the front returned to trenches.
  - id: ai-terminal-guidance
    name: AI terminal guidance
    start: 2023-06
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 40
    phases: 1
    tags: [ai, drones]
    description: Drones that find their target on their own for the last stretch, when the link is jammed.
  - id: mass-drone-production
    name: Mass drone production
    start: 2023-12
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 42
    phases: 1
    tags: [industry, drones]
    description: Millions of drones a year, built in small workshops as much as in factories.
  - id: fibre-optic-drones
    name: Fibre-optic drones
    start: 2024-08
    stop: 2032-01
    row: 46
    phases: 1
    tags: [drones, ew]
    description: Drones steered through a trailing fibre, immune to jamming.
  - id: ground-robots
    name: Uncrewed ground vehicles
    start: 2024-06
    stop: 2038-01
    row: 44
    phases: 1
    tags: [drones, logistics, upcoming]
    description: Robots carrying supplies and the wounded where a vehicle with a crew would be seen.
  - id: interceptor-drones
    name: Interceptor drones
    start: 2025-01
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 48
    phases: 1
    tags: [drones, air-defence]
    description: Cheap drones that hunt the attacking drones.
  - id: drone-walls
    name: Drone walls
    start: 2025-10
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 50
    phases: 1
    tags: [air-defence, policy, upcoming]
    description: Europe's plan for a belt of sensors and interceptors along its eastern border.
  - id: laser-air-defence
    name: Laser air defence
    start: 2026-06
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 52
    phases: 1
    tags: [air-defence, upcoming]
    description: Directed energy against drones, at the cost of electricity rather than a missile.
  - id: autonomous-drone-swarms
    name: Autonomous drone swarms
    start: 2027-01
    stop: 2042-01
    row: 54
    phases: 1
    tags: [drones, ai, conceptual]
  - id: human-machine-teams
    name: Human-machine combat teams
    start: 2028-01
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 56
    phases: 1
    tags: [ai, doctrine, conceptual]
    description: Units in which soldiers direct many robots, and the rules for who decides what.
triggers:
  - id: annexation-of-crimea
    name: Annexation of Crimea
    date: 2014-03
    row: 11
    tags: [doctrine]
    description: Unmarked troops and information operations took Crimea with little fighting.
  - id: mh17
    name: Downing of MH17
    date: 2014-07
    row: 15
    tags: [intelligence]
    description: Open-source investigators traced the missile launcher from photographs and videos posted online.
  - id: notpetya
    name: NotPetya cyberattack
    date: 2017-06
    row: 7
    tags: [cyber]
    description: Malware spread through Ukrainian accounting software and disabled companies worldwide.
  - id: second-nagorno-karabakh-war
    name: Second Nagorno-Karabakh War
    date: 2020-09
    row: 17
    tags: [drones]
    description: Forty-four days in which strike drones and loitering munitions destroyed armour and air defences.
  - id: full-scale-invasion
    name: Full-scale invasion
    date: 2022-02
    row: 21
    tags: [doctrine]
    description: Russia's invasion of Ukraine on 24 February 2022.
  - id: sinking-of-moskva
    name: Sinking of the cruiser Moskva
    date: 2022-04
    row: 33
    tags: [naval]
    description: The Black Sea Fleet's flagship sank after a missile strike, and the fleet moved away from Ukraine's coast.
  - id: operation-spiderweb
    name: Operation Spiderweb
    date: 2025-06
    row: 41
    tags: [drones]
    description: Drones launched from trucks deep inside Russia struck strategic bombers at several airbases.
